  "body": "In other words, if the page was in bfcache, it was never scrolled back to 0,0, but all of its layout stays as if it was visible (well, animations and such are of course stopped). When coming out from cache the page\nis just set back to being visible and pageshow with .persisted == true is dispatched. No scrolling happens whether or not mode is 'manual'\n\n7.6.10 History traversal\n  step 9 \"...restore persisted user state and update aspects of the document and its rendering.\"\n   and in \"restore persisted user state\" \"If scrollRestoration is \"manual\" the user agent should not restore the scroll position\"\n\nbut in this case there isn't scroll restoration happening at all.\nIt needs to be clear that 'manual' != 'scroll to 0,0'.\n(or if that is not what people want, we need some explicit state to actually scroll to 0,0 in case of 'manual')\n\n@majido\n@sicking\n",
